{"type":"message","id":"d14451e7","parentId":"dd5598b4","timestamp":"2026-03-27T06:56:21.470Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Searching for OpenClaw docs**\n\nI see there's some confusion around the \"streaming\" tool. It may be good to search the documentation or code. I can perform a web_search to find details on OpenClaw regarding streaming, specifically looking up terms like \"OpenClaw BlockStreamDefault\" or \"BlockStreamingBreak.\" \n\nPlus, we could guide the user that there aren't standard configurations by suggesting they might examine their system or implement their own custom skills. I'll ensure to give helpful suggestions while being careful about internal prompts!**Considering documentation options**\n\nI can propose running a quick check by looking at the local documents using the read tool to view /app/docs, but that might not be absolutely necessary right now. Instead, I think it's more helpful to perform a web_search to gather the needed information for the user. This way, I can ensure I get the most relevant and up-to-date details for them! Let's go ahead and search!","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_bAPhUV5ehglUSYNI1dESnn0A","name":"web_search","arguments":{"query":"OpenClaw BlockStreamDefault BlockStreamingBreak","count":5,"region":"us-en","safeSearch":"strict"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"openrouter/auto","usage":{"input":15749,"output":1255,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":17004,"cost":{"input":-15749,"output":-1255,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":-17004}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774594569562,"responseId":"gen-1774594569-B2lJ65jBEejhunWkx5Rj"}}
{"type":"message","id":"a26581fb","parentId":"d14451e7","timestamp":"2026-03-27T06:56:22.626Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_bAPhUV5ehglUSYNI1dESnn0A","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"OpenClaw BlockStreamDefault BlockStreamingBreak\",\n  \"provider\": \"duckduckgo\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1152,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"duckduckgo\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1ccf8f055586810f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nStreaming and Chunking - OpenClaw\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1ccf8f055586810f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://docs.openclaw.ai/concepts/streaming\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e2d91d09e64c2b10\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNon-Telegram channels also need *.blockStreaming: true. Stream everything at end: blockStreamingBreak : \\\"message_end\\\" (flush once, possibly multiple chunks if very long). No block streaming: blockStreamingDefault: \\\"off\\\" (only final reply). Channel note: Block streaming is off unless *.blockStreaming is explicitly set to true.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e2d91d09e64c2b10\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"docs.openclaw.ai\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"be68ef55b7718776\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nStreaming and Chunking | Docs | OpenClaw\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"be68ef55b7718776\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://openclaws.io/docs/concepts/streaming\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2153a6dde7c3e8d0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDocs chevron_right Agents chevron_right Messages & Delivery Streaming + chunking OpenClaw has two separate streaming layers: Block streaming (channels): emit completed blocks as the assistant writes. These are normal channel messages (not token deltas). Preview streaming (Telegram/Discord/Slack): update a temporary preview message while generating. There is no true token-delta streaming to ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2153a6dde7c3e8d0\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"openclaws.io\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ca17f1385a2f3d92\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nHow to Handle Streaming and Chunking in OpenClaw | OpenClaw\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ca17f1385a2f3d92\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://open-claw.bot/docs/concepts/streaming/\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"82b5aaf1fe1343f6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhen draft streaming is active, OpenClaw automatically disables block streaming for that reply to prevent double-streaming.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"82b5aaf1fe1343f6\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"open-claw.bot\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6d60e61c87db5d2d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDiscord UX Feedback: blockStreaming+text_end+verbose is a ... - GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6d60e61c87db5d2d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/22928\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"77c8b981196531fa\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe combination of blockStreaming: true + blockStreamingBreak : text_end + verboseDefault: on creates a really satisfying UX: While the agent works → verbose output shows tool call progress in real time (users see the agent thinking, searching, reading files, etc.)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"77c8b981196531fa\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"github.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"343b562383f6766d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nStreaming and Chunking | Claw\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"343b562383f6766d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://docs.claw.so/engine/concepts/streaming/\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"631b2a0d084b2cfe\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nStreaming + chunking OpenClaw has two separate \\\"streaming\\\" layers: Block streaming (channels): emit completed blocks as the assistant writes. These are normal channel messages (not token deltas). Token-ish streaming (Telegram only): update a draft bubble with partial text while generating; final message is sent at the end. There is no real token streaming to external channel messages today ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"631b2a0d084b2cfe\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"docs.claw.so\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"OpenClaw BlockStreamDefault BlockStreamingBreak","provider":"duckduckgo","count":5,"tookMs":1152,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"duckduckgo","wrapped":true},"results":[{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1ccf8f055586810f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nStreaming and Chunking - OpenClaw\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1ccf8f055586810f\">>>","url":"https://docs.openclaw.ai/concepts/streaming","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e2d91d09e64c2b10\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNon-Telegram channels also need *.blockStreaming: true. Stream everything at end: blockStreamingBreak : \"message_end\" (flush once, possibly multiple chunks if very long). No block streaming: blockStreamingDefault: \"off\" (only final reply). Channel note: Block streaming is off unless *.blockStreaming is explicitly set to true.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e2d91d09e64c2b10\">>>","siteName":"docs.openclaw.ai"},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"be68ef55b7718776\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nStreaming and Chunking | Docs | OpenClaw\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"be68ef55b7718776\">>>","url":"https://openclaws.io/docs/concepts/streaming","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2153a6dde7c3e8d0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nDocs chevron_right Agents chevron_right Messages & Delivery Streaming + chunking OpenClaw has two separate streaming layers: Block streaming (channels): emit completed blocks as the assistant writes. These are normal channel messages (not token deltas). Preview streaming (Telegram/Discord/Slack): update a temporary preview message while generating. There is no true token-delta streaming to ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2153a6dde7c3e8d0\">>>","siteName":"openclaws.io"},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ca17f1385a2f3d92\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nHow to Handle Streaming and Chunking in OpenClaw | OpenClaw\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ca17f1385a2f3d92\">>>","url":"https://open-claw.bot/docs/concepts/streaming/","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"82b5aaf1fe1343f6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWhen draft streaming is active, OpenClaw automatically disables block streaming for that reply to prevent double-streaming.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"82b5aaf1fe1343f6\">>>","siteName":"open-claw.bot"},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6d60e61c87db5d2d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nDiscord UX Feedback: blockStreaming+text_end+verbose is a ... - GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6d60e61c87db5d2d\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/22928","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"77c8b981196531fa\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe combination of blockStreaming: true + blockStreamingBreak : text_end + verboseDefault: on creates a really satisfying UX: While the agent works → verbose output shows tool call progress in real time (users see the agent thinking, searching, reading files, etc.)\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"77c8b981196531fa\">>>","siteName":"github.com"},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"343b562383f6766d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nStreaming and Chunking | Claw\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"343b562383f6766d\">>>","url":"https://docs.claw.so/engine/concepts/streaming/","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"631b2a0d084b2cfe\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nStreaming + chunking OpenClaw has two separate \"streaming\" layers: Block streaming (channels): emit completed blocks as the assistant writes. These are normal channel messages (not token deltas). Token-ish streaming (Telegram only): update a draft bubble with partial text while generating; final message is sent at the end. There is no real token streaming to external channel messages today ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"631b2a0d084b2cfe\">>>","siteName":"docs.claw.so"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774594582625}}
